request.description:
Three asks: soil answered, gold refused, potato price missing a district. `location` is omitted deliberately.

`status` is `answered` because something was answered. `refused[]` and `missing[]` both carry data — this is the case the flat terminal schema exists for.

Expected frames:

```
event: claim
data: {"text":"Potato grows best in well-drained sandy loam soil.","source_id":"1"}

event: claim
data: {"text":"Keep soil pH between 5.2 and 6.4.","source_id":"1"}

event: claim
data: {"text":"I cannot help with gold prices.","source_id":null}

event: claim
data: {"text":"Which district should I check potato prices for?","source_id":null}

event: turn.completed
data: {"status":"answered","cause":null,"text":"…","sources":[{"id":"1","name":"ICAR Potato Guide","kind":"document","url":"…"}],"confidence":"high","limitations":[],"refused":[{"what":"gold prices","reason":"outside agriculture"}],"missing":[{"name":"market.state"}],"trace_id":"trc_minted"}
```

